# Push changes to GitHub

When a task changes files in this repo, commit those changes and push them to GitHub before finishing.

- Stage only the files for the task. Do not commit secrets or local caches.
- Write a short commit message that matches the repo style and says why the change was made.
- Push the current branch to `origin`. Do not force-push.
- If the commit or push fails, fix the problem and create a new commit. Do not amend a rejected commit.
